  "prefLabel": "Plc 202.24 Prosecutor",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 202.24 “Prosecutor” means the individual appointed by the OPLC to present the evidence collected in an investigation in a proceeding arising from allegations of licensee misconduct or unlicensed practice. The term includes “administrative prosecutor”.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Plc 200) #13427, eff 8-4-22; ss by #13837, eff 12-28-23 (formerly Plc 202.20) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Plc 200); ss by #14136, eff 12-1-24 (formerly Plc 202.34)",
